COAX_WORK_DETAILS :: "65b7|65b710d3add3022d9f4b77e793da9ea1432710c33a0119b4d212cba956fee94b||The main Coax roadmap: what gets built in what order so OpenAgents and Metareal can express computation, data, protocols, tools and build policy in Coax, with costs and ownership visible. Milestones have dependencies and exit evidence, not dates.\\n\\nSpecification: coax/ROADMAP.md in the openagents repository.||\n6f40|6f40bdaaf4012eddd207f37bd5269b7300cb47d982738a2981433b500ffc8f35||Real engine kernels and the whole development loop measured against frozen references, original-source debugging, one release/status source and an independently enforced review gate. Exit: reproducible kernel and whole-loop reports, no unexpected output or allocation regressions, usable native debugging, a versioned baseline.||\nd98b|d98bd18d14eb90c38974a688a4d41d3917764e2a8a69fd5082dca321a24681cb||R1a first: declaration and content identities, explicit targets, original spans, basic namespaces and inspectable procedure lowering, pinned by differential fixtures. R1b scheduling and configuration follow.||\n08f5|08f57f4e5b411eee3cea11793e980103f99b6afb6d2afc45211d9b93046e855c||R2a first: tagged results and optionals, exhaustive switching, propagation and cleanup; a shared asynchronous host contract with R3.||\n27ad|27ad3acadab3d706b6accf79869f8d2eea208d65e92768a7782aaa8eadba8b4a||R3a started (E0383 rejects simple returns of borrows into local arrays). Then typed transfer, deferred destruction and owning storage (R3b).||\na0eb|a0eb08dcf5fe3170ed7f027b1aeadbc74dfaf86fb94eaa32634f5bbd014e7065||R4a first: generic copyable values and non-owning operations over fixed storage; owning libraries wait for R3b.||\n265f|265f90e30e9a84da1061c584a4b233dc5117f000fcd289bcbf518d9d28a35075||R5a first: narrow derivation over concrete, already-checked types.||\n1ca0|1ca0f77a097e3a712ed32ce996a2d73c0535b0da6a6923ad1a7b2311eeb29a34||Phase-typed Code, quotation, #insert and #expand with hygiene and expansion budgets.||\na989|a9896a04fd5c4adb8f4e3697e37f59328f0ce7c5db0b5944f68185f4fa6623d2||R7a: formatting, evidence, typed queries and revision-bound fixes early, on current APIs. R7b: workspaces, typed plugins and build programming.||\nc1fb|c1fbb24e4aa29cd70974f45bfafbf085838187a5b066eccad77b34fc8f1b9dd8||R8a target-specific GPU interfaces; R8b a browser vertical slice (Coaxial is the wasm32 probe).||\n09a3|09a36809f54c8b000eeb983ae16838bdfb11b6a9d6b2621a5a65f46a74351fab||Transitive effect summaries for allocation, host I/O, clocks and randomness; strict math; deterministic jobs.||\ncd0d|cd0d1ea4a618997d6af848f9514bc6e5a3247eaadee5df6df3b76b41a137002d||The remaining semantic work moves into Coax in reviewable slices.||\n3daf|3dafb6d9d2eb1c2bd4d46ad572a9aea0808d0611a2afe3d5034a2bbbb478aede||R11a restricted procedure-body replacement (unchanged-layout Mac experiment first); R11b resident semantics and transactional migration.||\nff44|ff44560d1891c10bf3c7a6a0d0e47fdcbeff0063086ec6528c1b76736f764c3c||The C backend stays the reference; a fast native debug backend only when profiling shows C compilation is the bottleneck.||\n47b1|47b1de82fd67af95ad4ce28f2164dc8812c48fd30ae27cec4b49f99aa824c2e0||Shipped in df008f96a4: generic host socket open/send/close, bounded text frames and open/frame/close/error inbox messages. socket.coax and project-live.coax exercise subscriptions, reconnect and a real frame counter. Task rows still use verified build-time snapshots; parsed live folding, Coax signature verification and NIP-42 readiness remain separate open tasks.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/web/host.js\\n- apps/openagents-web/ui.coax|Retain the socket.coax and project-live.coax scripted inbox/open/frame/close/error checks from df008f96a4\\.The committed real-page frame counter probe connects to relay.openagents.com; no live task-fold claim is implied|10-28 15:11 CDT\\:claude-live-1\\:Probe narrowed: the probe page is /project/coax itself; its header chip drew the frame count (198 frames from relay.openagents.com in headless Chrome). Ids: socket_open(url) returns 0..3 or -1; events are message kinds 256 + 4*id + event (0 opened, 1 frame, 2 closed, 3 error). The C face drains a Coax command queue into the imports, since #foreign takes scalars only.\\.10-28 15:11 CDT\\:claude-live-1\\:Done in df008f96a4: https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/df008f96a4\nd223|d2231dfceab3e2e404cb4c4bcf29a0d11ae02857a5ba4fbb1ee0331384b2e14d||Shipped in 8f23a77f35: bounded Coax JSON pull parser/writer, UTF-8 and escape handling, fixed input/depth/string limits, 267 JSONTestSuite cases and captured-relay native trapping-allocator tests. Its json_int admits 2^53 and duplicate object keys are not domain-policy checked. New profile/duplicate/safe-integer hardening is a separate task, not a claim that this parser did not ship.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/json.coax|Retain the committed JSONTestSuite/captured-relay/native no-allocation regressions from 8f23a77f35\\.Coax event-domain conformance and new consumer limits are explicitly not established by this resolved parser task|10-28 15:16 CDT\\:claude-live-1\\:JSONTestSuite 1ef36fa pinned: 267 y_/n_ cases in coax/lib/nostr/fixtures/json_suite.coax; 16 left out (not UTF-8, over 4 KiB, or a control byte a Coax literal can't hold), listed in the file; json.coax's own tests cover bad UTF-8 byte by byte and depth 17. No-allocation check: coax/tests/nostr.py CoaxJsonTests links it with a malloc/calloc/realloc/free that abort and parses all 212 captured frames.\\.10-28 15:16 CDT\\:claude-live-1\\:Done in 8f23a77f35: https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/8f23a77f35\nc29a|c29a2169fbe2992a82613bd23599354fa629e325e7131fb5f7d79974aabdd0c2|10-28 15:17 CDT|Extend the shipped socket/frame probe: parse bounded relay JSON, retain project-scoped events and fold issues/revisions/status/comments/plans/order in Coax. Reconnect/catch-up with missing dependencies explicit. Existing signature-verified snapshot is first paint. Until project-page-verify, live rows are explicitly relay-trusted provisional data, cannot overwrite verified state or feed authority/claims; LIVE means socket state only.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- apps/openagents-web/project.coax\\n- apps/openagents-web/projects/coax/|Throwaway signed claim/plan/status/order on a local relay redraws the page within 2s without release; captured fixtures agree with model.ts\\.Provisional and verified snapshot states stay distinct; malformed/out-of-scope/missing/deferred events never become authoritative\\.Reconnect, partial EOSE, capacity and old-generation tests pass; check-visuals passes|\nb554|b554abc876c574f63cbf357b55bd2ed7feb8303be2892e717877bd239d7505d7||The cast pose, robots/body capsules and player collision run through a repeatable C ABI harness against a pinned native reference (coax0 0.13.0).\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.||10-28 15:03 CDT\\:codex-coax\\:Done in 4830ad9c30: https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/4830ad9c30ef749d12c75cb57e35ea7ecff2ff2f\nd8c8|d8c8a4d1122f00c9d9c575c6b59dd1befc5d496763deb813d6068fdd6b366059||LLDB breakpoints, stepping, values, stacks, diagnostics and sanitizer traces map to Coax source on Mac and a Simulator app (coax0 0.13.0).\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.||10-28 15:03 CDT\\:codex-coax\\:Done in 4830ad9c30: https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/4830ad9c30ef749d12c75cb57e35ea7ecff2ff2f\n9527|95273c87481fc686aa436c637bcb90fb658c94570b989e8cc686adcc2da0c03e||The Coax pose kernel passes the unchanged 5% median gate: 1.034x native unoptimized, 0.807x app profile, 0.740x release; reference, harness and budget frozen.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.||10-28 15:03 CDT\\:codex-coax\\:Done in ff83c9d959: https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/ff83c9d959f2d9d94b676b16a441039c30c7f569\n7c2f|7c2f5867576bf90374a3264acbea6039e72d660b8eeb8e8d676d8ca584d9b5c6|10-28 15:03 CDT|CLI version, accepted-feature tables and book status generated from one source, with a publication drift check; implementation, schema and introduction versions kept distinct.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|Version, feature tables and book status are generated, not hand-edited\\.A drift check fails when a published copy disagrees with the source|10-28 15:03 CDT\\:codex-coax\\:Codex thread 01a17379 is on this now (single-source release/status generation and drift checks), with a subagent on another roadmap slice.\n57b3|57b3bc4877bf63ea786de351f3616835ffce903546500fda8bdeefc38457fc5f||Agree a frame-tail budget, then measure the Coax kernels on a named phone: CPU time, tails, copies, allocations and GPU upload, with raw results and dispersion retained.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|A tail budget is written down before optimizing\\.Device runs retained with dispersion; the owner's device step is in NEEDS_OWNER.md|\nd383|d3838817c77b34f32eb9006479c4cebb108e1c73a327b8d602da0ba436e8ded2||Load/parse/check, compile-time work, generation, C compilation, link, assets, launch and GPU preparation; generated C size and peak compiler memory.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|A report attributes every stage for clean and warm builds\\.The largest bottleneck is named with its numbers|\n9d2e|9d2e29f53d1ab109714ebaa9f38cf47c8fcbd14c51218099511930f244ecfa54||Define who reviews changes to invariants, oracles and verification policy, enforced outside the compiler on owned infrastructure, including moves into unmarked helpers.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|The policy is written and enforced by a check outside the compiler\\.A change that weakens a check and its code together is refused without review|\nc296|c296d48f949f9decc5f96333e8d34b113ff066c08a40fbb51af21223c00fdaff||A versioned design and migration for checked arithmetic with explicit wrapping, profile metadata in artifacts and cache keys, and same-profile unoptimized/optimized conformance vectors (overflow, casts, shifts, division edges, evaluation order, cleanup, f32 literal rounding).\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|Profiles recorded in artifact metadata\\.Conformance vectors pass in both optimization levels|\nccba|ccba52ff7f1b14e8beb1f74deef63ab443c5dfe4fd80deab1369bc5cb45b8446||An optional native check executable runs pinned inputs through the evaluator and the emitted unoptimized and optimized procedures and compares values, traps and buffer writes.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|Seeded evaluator/emitter defects are caught\\.Mismatches minimised and kept as regressions|\n3c97|3c97013cfd742dccd08ffc61f5ef2987590d2bcf3d27a35a3fb228ca00303f57||Every claim bound to source, compiler, target, profile, selection and budgets, with outcomes passed, counterexample, inconclusive, infrastructure error and not checked.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|coax test and coax mutate write the record\\.Missing execution is never a pass|\nf535|f53502bac1b51795d1e3c859655a73d663418b065082d9881662add29ce18c6e||Change a kernel, add a field, repair a type error, update a protocol adapter; pinned revisions, tools and budgets; measure accepted completion, repair iterations and edit-to-result time.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|Four tasks pinned with oracles agents can't edit\\.A first run's numbers recorded|\n963b|963ba9fc751a7e575ad782f6635f6bcafca01bd3b5567d4990f3b95e6385cecb||Declaration and content identities, explicit target descriptions, original spans, basic namespaces and minimal inspectable procedure lowering, pinned with differential fixtures and independent oracles.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|Differential fixtures pass against independent oracles|\nca69|ca69f93a896a77f083747dc30d49d5de3420f174748ced153f5ed6aafd9b5ccd||coax fmt and evidence reporting using today's compiler APIs; typed queries and revision-bound fixes follow R1a.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|coax fmt is idempotent over the repository's Coax files|\n07c2|07c2bc1acfda2ce3c5cd3c98b17836e42c3a541171ac557bf4cb2067bf8a6b70||E0383 rejects straightforward local-array view and string returns.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.||10-28 15:03 CDT\\:codex-coax\\:Done in 9d0f246ba1: https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/9d0f246ba1b95ae0a491cce8e6cb15f4a1de3d21\n6541|6541812581360075e6a12e196f4773d4ab5c4a90b39a409098eb60f916833c80||Typed results and optionals, exhaustive switch, propagation and exhaustive cleanup, with one real asynchronous adapter.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|The spec's R2a examples compile and their checks pass|\n76ba|76bad4951d0c2dc57eda7e4522070c27e951ab21a06177f05f1c5f0368b273b7||Generic copyable values and non-owning operations over fixed storage.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.||\n791f|791f07997d9b98b2a86b2f3157fcd71db650fca9cfa838f634998d3bbc9d92ee||Narrow derivation (equality, formatting, serialization) over concrete, already-checked types.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.||\n0c13|0c13c6ed2696572356537f5a6b8340b3431a779cae2f96ae1bbb5df6f6f3f414||The unchanged-layout Mac replacement experiment: swap a procedure body in a running app.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.||\n9680|968040980c4cc123132f11495fc8b6279fadc183015b1b17bf2026b1e02f89e9||Shared iOS vectors, device-only Keychain software-key custody, NIP-46 permissions/lifecycle, QR and NIP-98 sessions. Throwaway tests first; production identity waits for review.||\ndd90|dd902da03d8d43e06d3f88e7d043e42449957f077f825693fc9e6022a43c9d07||8x32 scalar arithmetic modulo n with explicit split-product/carry scheduling and compile-time bounds for each accumulator: one 32x32 product fits u64 but a sum may overflow. Canonical load/store, overflow/zero checks, add/mul/negate/inverse and windows; secret-path reduction is branch/index independent.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/crypto/secp_scalar.coax|Compile-time bound checks cover multiplication/reduction intermediates; seeded carry loss is caught\\.0, 1, n-1, n, 2^256-1 and 1000000 random operations match the independent oracle\\.Checked/optimized results agree; zero surviving mutants|\n8ee9|8ee9d948eb3062e4ecb6755c77113f4926f306216c14b8230c686dcad6c1cbc4||Affine/Jacobian points, lifts and validation, add/double/mixed operations and masked table selection. Specify complete formulas or masked exceptional handling for secret paths including P=Q, P=-Q, infinity and invalid points; verification-only variable-time helpers are separate.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/crypto/secp_group.coax|Independent generator/random points and infinity/P=Q/P=-Q/invalid-lift cases match\\.Secret-path exceptional inputs never select secret branches/indices; zero surviving mutants|\nff0f|ff0f3e69b0a60bd5f4bff2ddd7c5e46a053c3e7036eb6b84bed7f1f28e26995e||coax/lib/crypto/secp_mult.coax: ecmult_vartime(a, P, b) using wNAF (window 5 for P, a precomputed G table generated with #run). Public inputs only; name ends _vartime.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/crypto/secp_mult.coax|100,000 random (a, P, b) match the harness\\.Precomputed table generated at compile time within the step budget|\n41bd|41bdfb8f0861f587a6f0b7b8aa9e47b854da9dde7e1d659913eb0ac28e94926c||General byte-view BIP-340 verification plus a Nostr wrapper for a 32-byte event ID. Refuse invalid lifts, r>=p, s>=n and malformed lengths. Read-only verification does not depend on signing, keys, AUTH or erasure.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/crypto/schnorr.coax|All 19 official verification rows including message lengths 0, 1, 17 and 100 match\\.A one-hour differential run vs pinned libsecp retains seeds and regressions\\.Record native/Wasm verify time and actual target/profile; performance cannot waive correctness|\n6943|69431a57b1c90581f1d71cbf5139e9413287fd9aefb0616548c3d7bed6f1333b||Dev-only real-event probe using the actual shared canonical event reader/ID serializer/verifier, not a second minimal implementation. Baked public fixture, no signing or production key dependency.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- apps/openagents-web/|ID/content/signature tampering and out-of-profile input show REFUSED; an independently verified real fixture shows VERIFIED\\.Visuals check passes; no signing dependency in this task closure|\n94a3|94a3347135a6feb30e2745a0f244f338d986842dfe4c34cb95280fd38899d34f||Comb method with a table generated by #run (32 KB variant for the page, 64 KB native); every lookup through ge_table_select; no secret branches.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/crypto/secp_mult.coax|100000 random scalars and boundary scalars match the independent oracle\\.Record actual table-generation budget and emitted table/stack size\\.Timing probe reports no detected leakage for the declared native profile; generated-code audit remains separate|\n3e29|3e29fd0e72622bf43e24cd33daf0c6c457f4d81317111a98ee0707ffdf67c62b||A fixed-window (4-bit) constant-time multiplication for ECDH, with signed-digit recoding and masked table selection.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/crypto/secp_mult.coax|100000 random scalar/peer pairs and exceptional points match\\.Secret branches/indices are forbidden by the documented source scope; timing probe records methodology without claiming proof|\n51f4|51f416c58a9c0b1b034d374a7fec805de9d9864211814cd792831113ab0f53a8||General byte-view BIP-340 sign(message,seckey32,aux32), with a Nostr 32-byte wrapper. Validate 1<=key<n, parity normalization, auxiliary randomness, zero nonce refusal and final self-verification. Caller-owned bounded scratch and failure wiping; no partial signature released.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/crypto/schnorr.coax|All official signing rows match byte for byte including non-32-byte messages\\.Invalid/zero key, zero nonce and injected self-verification failure release no signature and wipe owned scratch\\.Checked/optimized/native/Wasm results agree; timing is no-detected-leak evidence, not proof|\n71e7|71e7df5f2935d6e8e3a9cd8cbafcdd25b743b9064d891661fff41271a271de0f||Validated raw shared x for NIP-44: refuse invalid peer points/scalars/infinity. The libsecp oracle must supply the raw-x callback; default secp256k1_ecdh hashes a compressed point and is the wrong oracle.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/crypto/ecdh.coax|Official conversation-key and labelled adapted Wycheproof cases agree with independent raw-x computation\\.Seeded use of the default libsecp hash callback is detected; error paths wipe scratch|\n0bd1|0bd17619f83ed2dc6152e607c9aca14402a83a589be838a6d80ca18f99db0b0d||tools/coax-nostr/timing/: fixed-vs-random class runs with Welch's t-test, native (Apple silicon and x86-64) and a wasm32 report mode.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- tools/coax-nostr/timing/|Seeded secret-branch/index leakage is detected with retained class counts/statistics and noise conditions\\.Declared native arm64/x86-64 runs record at least 10^6 samples and t statistics; no-detected-leak is never labelled a proof\\.Wasm browser results are reported by engine/tier/flags with no universal timing guarantee|\n4878|48783672d1a1652b41951c641f8331bcd3c574549b481196abb3251529dfb167||Pinned NIP-44 v2 conversation/message keys, padding and ChaCha20/HMAC. MAC authenticates nonce\\p\\pciphertext before plaintext release; caller supplies fresh entropy. Support the six-byte prefix at >=65536 or explicitly refuse it under a named bounded profile. Outer event verification is mandatory at the signed-event integration boundary.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/nip44.coax|All upstream valid/invalid vectors and 65535/65536/65537 extended-prefix boundary fixtures pass or produce the advertised capacity refusal\\.Wrong MAC/version/nonce/padding/alias/capacity never releases plaintext; zero surviving mutants\\.Independent encrypt/decrypt interoperability in both directions, with no production key|\nef5a|ef5aa35ce36cfdd1bf6ed0c89e20ebaa292e896adedf1fb553e03c4f6204a432||coax/lib/nostr/nip59.coax: build rumor (unsigned), seal (kind 13, signed by author, NIP-44 to recipient), wrap (kind 1059 from a fresh key, randomized created_at within two days back); unwrap verifies wrap sig, decrypts, verifies seal sig and that rumor pubkey equals seal pubkey.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/nip59.coax|Independent wrap/seal interoperability in both directions, including the existing test deck\\.Reject altered outer signature, bad seal signature, rumor identity mismatch, missing recipient and oversized private payload\\.Fresh wrap keys/nonces/timestamp policy and failure cleanup are covered|\n78f3|78f3558f1975babb59910e79b424de75f48dd60a8154557f6531729820acb088||A native test that fetches the sealed test deck's wrap fixture (checked in from the scratch e2e, test deck only), unwraps it with the recipient test key, checks the 3188 envelope digest and prints the slide titles.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- tools/coax-nostr/tests/|Prints the two test-deck slide titles; digest matches|\n7cdf|7cdf2fe4a30442eba7a02e6eeafe44f90b64e24eb7fd9e231280d1f11b34e753||Read-only parse, exact NIP-01 canonical ID serialization/hash and BIP-340 verification with profile limits. Preserve original JSON, ordered tags, unknown fields and exact content. Freshness is consumer admission, not signature validity. Signing moves to nostr-event-sign so verified public reads do not wait for secret-key features.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/event.coax|Escape/non-ASCII/astral/empty-tag preimages match independent event-hash implementations\\.Altered fields/ID/signature, invalid point, malformed/duplicate keys and capacity refusals have negative vectors\\.The task dependency closure contains no signing, keys or NIP-42 task|\n9413|941365238306bf0600e998a145f98b31010de2ce773b52cfee524c115b88b9e2||coax/lib/nostr/filter.coax: ids, authors, kinds, #<tag>, since, until, limit; serialize to JSON and match an event locally (to drop events a relay shouldn't have sent).\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/filter.coax|#test matrix of filter x event matches NIP-01 semantics|\n8ccd|8ccd826b7e26625fa02fdef67065f80e033e23d28fa419e7e8c9680c57cd2e5c||BIP-173 bech32 (not bech32m) and NIP-19 npub/nsec/note/TLV entities with source-specific limits and unknown-type handling. Decode nsec only into caller-owned secret buffers, with explicit lifecycle supplied by keys.coax.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/bech32.coax|BIP-173 valid/invalid vectors and NIP-19 examples agree with independent codecs\\.10000 random entities plus unknown TLV/length/capacity cases agree; nsec never logged|\n5923|592367e138a305e3e9348b2178b80dba13d7cfbf9fa5f095529f507f14014b73||Explicit integer-only RFC8785 envelope profile: UTF-16 member ordering, exact string rules and safe-integer bounds, preserving original input. Refuse floats/out-of-range integers instead of claiming general JCS support.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/jcs.coax|Independent integer-only/astral-key/safe-number boundary fixtures agree\\.Unsupported numeric values refuse; existing test-deck envelope digest remains byte-identical|\nfdce|fdce7d97951b382e2d14adec11c47a90ddfad1987a5c19d9cfef0619d30f637f||coax/lib/nostr/envelope.coax: build and check openagents.artifact-envelope.v1 (inline body, digest = SHA-256 of JCS bytes, 1 MiB cap) per nips/openagents/contracts.md.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/envelope.coax|Builds byte-identical envelopes to coax/web/unlock/lib.ts for the test deck\\.Refuses a digest mismatch and an oversize body|\nd0d7|d0d77f68357bf14ddf77a52687a8305cbeff29d616c315d021290f7bede0bac2||coax/web/host.js: random(ptr, len) from crypto.getRandomValues (chunked at 65,536 bytes); a page without it refuses to run crypto.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/web/host.js|Browser CSPRNG adapter fills requested lengths including >65536 through chunking\\.Unavailable entropy/invalid spans fail closed with no clock/Math.random fallback; deterministic injection exists only in test API|\n44fe|44fe38068474bb38e4943023b7752418e8ab8eab89edea791e9702883ce9aa1b||store_put/get/delete over one IndexedDB object store per origin; results via the inbox; private browsing failure reported, not thrown.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/web/host.js|Put/reload/get/delete generation-safe byte transfers pass\\.Unavailable/quota/oversize/cancelled/late response states refuse cleanly; deleted records do not reappear|\n7de9|7de9620d9706743839185d429a0bdd1b25cd768c2d97d5f60025a697fda7475d||Pure bounded verified client machine with connection/subscription generations, REQ/CLOSE/EVENT/OK/EOSE/CLOSED/NOTICE/AUTH, acknowledgement deadlines, cancellation, duplicate suppression and capped jittered reconnect. AUTH-required retry is once per authenticated generation. EOSE/short page never claims completeness; public reads need not wait for AUTH when the relay permits them.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/relay.coax|Scripted transcripts cover ACK true/false/timeout, AUTH/reconnect, stale generations, duplicates, unknown subscriptions, queue overflow and forged events\\.No host I/O inside Coax state machine; profile limits have clean refusal states|\nf426|f4268f9b58bbf38358880298462c5958b0cbb59dfefca02ecb6c5303e40d3fc2||Bound kind22242 AUTH builder and signer handoff for current relay/challenge/connection generation. Proof of possession does not grant channel or host-operation authority.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/nip42.coax|Independent tags/signatures match; old challenge/relay/generation responses are refused|\nfd70|fd709fde9a20e47041f0fa1f491257a7c4bf832c527d10ac97a5149f7b2bfe13||SecretSlot/forget and versioned key records. Prefer phone/NIP-46 or NIP-07 signer; explicit local browser slots are ephemeral by default. No new plaintext nsec IndexedDB persistence. Durable encrypted exports wait for the optional NIP-49 task; document legacy unlock-store migration.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/keys.coax\\n- coax/web/host.js|Ephemeral slot import/forget and all error paths wipe bounded owned buffers; no key in logs/public state\\.Returned signer output is correlated and verified for identity/body/scope\\.Legacy storage migration/deletion failure states are explicit; no plaintext-persistence default|\n4cca|4cca7f4d3f587b3796ead071adb8ce12e2673e186e7dcc8e25e2037f573289ea||Wire host pipes and relay.coax into a probe page: connect, answer AUTH with a test key, subscribe to a known filter, draw verified event count and refusals.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- apps/openagents-web/|Probe on staging shows the expected count from relay.openagents.com\\.A REQ is never sent before AUTH completes (asserted from the outbox log)|\n4a73|4a73354378a9e7058ca56491bb7de0bed6ea1d80d8be1f82c92b94e10d882bb3||Replace coax/web/unlock/page.ts: fetch the wrap through relay.coax with AUTH as the recipient, unwrap with nip59.coax, check the envelope, hand slides to ui.coax.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- apps/openagents-web/\\n- coax/web/unlock/|The real phrase opens the deck on staging with page.ts removed\\.Wrong key shows the key-wrong state|\n51e6|51e676b7869c773966ca2761abb58dd2548847d72869e035fae8a55075b6a630||Implement only the independently reviewed versioned phrase-gate format, authenticated framing/domain separation/nonces/KDF bounds and dual-reader migration specified by unlock-gate-format. Existing AES-GCM adapter remains until cutover/rollback evidence exists.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- apps/openagents-web/\\n- coax/web/unlock/gate.ts|Pinned old/new fixtures, wrong phrase/MAC/version/nonce/length, oversize work and failure cleanup pass\\.Staging replacement preserves access during the declared window; rollback restores old readers/entries|\n5d1a|5d1af539c7ef817a326f1ff314008ae905c72700d07d924d5cece537cdcb92dd||tools/coax-nostr/: a native program built from the same modules: keygen, seal deck.md --author --to, gate (writes unlock entries for deploy.sh), publish (sign and send events to a relay with AUTH, using a small native socket), verify, fetch.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- tools/coax-nostr/\\n- coax/web/deploy.sh|deploy.sh runs the gate step with coax-nostr and no bun\\.Re-sealing the deck with coax-nostr opens on staging|\n97b8|97b87d0491b6420da9185339e5705d2478124c6d588de6b13d6af23507a60ca7||Change the INVARIANTS rule as coax/nostr.md 5 says, extend check-visuals.sh to refuse any page script besides host.js and any WebCrypto use, delete coax/web/unlock/, remove bun from deploy.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- INVARIANTS.md\\n- coax/web/check-visuals.sh\\n- coax/web/unlock/|Every old crypto/tool consumer has a verified replacement and rollback evidence before deletion\\.Check detects extra script/import/WebCrypto paths and seeded hidden dependency; coax/web/unlock retired only after cutover|\nce0b|ce0b851defc71422aea5845628d6f47c59b681505f712be0abf4766360a4c761||Replace the already-working TS publisher with native Coax tooling. Preserve every existing issue ID/slug, signed revision/status/plan history and project order. First publication has already shipped; this task is implementation migration, not creating duplicate issues.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- tools/coax-nostr/\\n- apps/openagents-web/projects/coax/work/|Readback signatures/IDs/fields agree with current publisher; existing issue IDs do not change\\.Second publish emits nothing; comments/plans/resolved states survive migration|\n4356|43563f5c9dbec79366f79a97141cb22c4561f83944616eab350e3996dfb14cc5||A signed-in authenticated worker requests an atomic COORD claim and displays its actual lease/fence. Existing project-key claim comments are informational history, not evidence of the worker identity. No claim before verified task state/admission.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- apps/openagents-web/|Two workers race for overlapping resources: exactly one grant, the other clean refusal\\.Renew/release/expiry and stale fence are tested; accepted claim appears on another browser within 5s|\ncf05|cf0533bafc8ef564549aa2cd792fb3d93db97e5c0631c3800c89c662a3253a0b||Optional GLV scalar decomposition only after actual verification arithmetic and a verified real-page benchmark exist. Not a blocker for core integration.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/crypto/secp_mult.coax|One-hour differential fuzz is clean with retained evidence\\.Record before/after Wasm verify distribution and size; accept optimization only with measured benefit|\na812|a812bca96c91845e93b0908ca34b456ba0750da412501313b6c0358d2228a191||Build the Coax Nostr modules (hashes, secp256k1, Schnorr, ECDH, NIP-44, events, bech32) as C for iOS arm64 and the simulator through the app's Generated/ build step, and run the shared vector files in the iOS test target. Report sign and verify times on a device.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- apps/openagents-ios/project.yml\\n- apps/openagents-ios/Tests/|Same BIP-340/NIP-44/event files pass via generated C on simulator and actual iOS arm64 when available\\.Entropy/ABI/lifetime/alias/error tests and simulator timings recorded; physical-device evidence is separately recorded, never inferred|\nbc0b|bc0bce463e952c08fc1ee63adca4818d6a1ca4666d9c3d38f4957bd2dfe4f192||Device-only Keychain storage, owner-approved create/import/export and per-operation/session user-presence policy. Coax secp256k1 software signing briefly exposes bounded secret memory; do not claim Secure Enclave isolation. Tests use throwaway keys. Production identity rollout waits for nostr-production-cutover.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- apps/openagents-ios/OpenAgents/|Simulator tests exercise create/import/sign/forget, denial and background timeout with throwaway keys\\.Device-only Keychain/user-presence settings and bounded key/copy wiping are inspected; no secret logs\\.Device owner step and production cutover prerequisite are recorded|\nbde1|bde19af6ec5d47fc841159be677d94f04b1002c837df352b2b949e15f1ffb99e||NIP-46 bunker side with distinct client/remote-signer/user identities, one-use connect secret and correlated kind24133 requests. Semantic permissions include kind+target+operation/scope/expiry, not a blanket kind allowlist. Unsupported NIP-04 methods return explicit errors.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/nip46.coax\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Independent client connect/get_public_key/sign_event/ping/nip44 round trips pass\\.Wrong/reused secret, identity confusion, ungranted target/scope, replay and altered returned event are refused\\.No production identity involved in development tests|\ncf39|cf3977ddddce49a1b04ca39289cb829a8f039848cd5c7961c961107f0935e4aa||The page side of Nostr Connect: an ephemeral client key, the nostrconnect:// URI (relay, secret, perms, name, url), waiting for the signer's connect, then get_public_key and sign_event requests over the page's relay client.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/nip46.coax\\n- apps/openagents-web/|In-memory independent client/signer round trips verify distinct signer/user keys and get_public_key\\.Relay switching/logout, duplicate IDs, timeout and late response behavior are explicit; ephemeral key wiped on sign-out|\n503d|503d16e4b775432544983bc1ce6da378ed209075fd3faf24d4e5384f28a1a3b8||Byte mode, error correction M, versions 1 to 15, mask selection by the standard penalty rules; output a module grid the page draws as HUD strokes or quads.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/qr/\\n- coax/tests/qr/|Matches a reference encoder's module grids for 20 fixed strings including a 300-byte nostrconnect URI\\.A phone camera (the iOS scanner test) decodes a rendered code|\na1d8|a1d85392c1cdcda73b83d8c22b82c959267620ea119aac3408b4e077dc0b13d1||The app's QR scanner recognises nostrconnect:// codes, shows the site and what it asks for in an approval sheet, and on approval runs the NIP-46 signer for that session; the session shows in Settings and can be ended there.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- apps/openagents-ios/OpenAgents/\\n- apps/openagents-ios/Tests/|Fixture QR opens owner approval; untrusted site metadata cannot grant permission\\.Deny/end-session/replay/suspension are tested; foreground resumption cannot approve an expired request|\n0af1|0af19f0b640e3bfc544a89722f0f5af6d9601dd5d2ebadbd28fccc54f8d7eac9||A native Coax server route POST /auth/nostr takes a NIP-98 kind 27235 event (url, method, payload hash, created_at within 60 s, unused id), verifies it with the Coax verifier, and sets an HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Strict session cookie bound to the pubkey. Admin pubkeys come from config. No WorkOS.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/nip98.coax\\n- tools/coax-nostr/server/|Valid throwaway login accepted; wrong URL/method/body/time/signature rejected\\.Replay reservation is atomic across workers and restart for the acceptance window\\.Bounded request/replay parsing has deterministic refusal; no key material in cookie|\nc8dd|c8ddf047e6f45e3cb209922826bd0a56284dbb200afff3c52b33cf566b927490||A Coaxial page draws the QR (HUD, Filament), waits for the phone, then asks it to sign the NIP-98 event and posts it to /auth/nostr. Shows who is signed in (npub, short) and sign out. Plain text in the hidden main for agents.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- apps/openagents-web/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Actual browser waiting/denied/signed-in/signed-out states pass with throwaway phone signer\\.User private key never enters browser memory; returned signatures are independently verified; visuals pass|\n73ce|73ce5c1cdf68fecacb68149159896ca1d245fe253597cde984cc61a0310aa7c4||The deliverable test: the iOS simulator scans the QR shown by the page (fixture image of the live page's code), approves, and the page reaches the signed-in state with the server session bound to the phone's pubkey. Device run is an owner step in NEEDS_OWNER.md.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- apps/openagents-ios/Tests/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/\\n- docs/verification/|Simulator plus browser and local relay/server pass happy path, refusal, replay and sign-out\\.Staging sign-in uses throwaway identity and exact origin/session binding\\.Physical-device approval/background evidence goes to NEEDS_OWNER.md; real identity requires production cutover|\nc969|c96951910dfb701627c5e9888c5265343c262f128b2471853a440fd3dc487aee||Verify each live event ID/signature and author/project scope in Coax before verified folding/storage. Bound pending work and spend <=4ms/frame; refuse/count forged events. Production verified mode consumes no relay-trusted provisional rows and has no signing/keys/AUTH dependency.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- apps/openagents-web/project.coax|A forged event via test relay never enters verified rows or downstream decisions; refusal/pending counts are visible\\.Signed project changes show in verified rows without release, with explicit incomplete/offline states\\.Actual Wasm browser transcript agrees with independent TS fold after verification|\ncead|ceadf04d205d5e97beaa1a998dfa4624706ad2cfdb59752c22780d0f364b27f0||Named limits, independent vectors/oracles, entropy, erasure, secret-path evidence and independent review. Foundation work starts first; production approval is a later gate, not a block on test-key development.||\n7d06|7d0670e71732845a879756718d75b7be8da3894ae1b8c5c409bb2fd725c12aa1||Verified event lifecycle, offline state, multi-relay catch-up, optional relay discovery and correlated signer requests.||\n100a|100a409bf2c25bad9e20e16bfad3766c43fea248d657e1c73517f0daffc87823||Use existing generated proto codecs with source evidence and policy; expand missing definitions only for real consumers.||\n7cbf|7cbfcd1ea5ae8c4f40b4fee889a96463e7320ea9330d82765b80d43b1b93202b||OA/AA current owner admission, selected asymmetric JWS/JWKS profiles, FI community policy and FA credential sessions.||\n5a3f|5a3fa1591068eadcdabc1891ca1ffcdda949ab5b7a261fafea23d87e1354f5ff||Scoped original grants, fresh authenticated routes, fenced worker claims, truthful task journals and a real Linux Codex task from the app.||\n752e|752ee6f8ae033e78d8d54a02db40a48785d0ea97e71a5a46c2415070646058c9||Live membership/visibility, CW bounded completeness, AR transactional history and IA consent.||\n3ae7|3ae7940f2b548295cd159565331fb6c6f2a69a60d7b7f3a30be861a710756eea||AE/AP/AO/AM privacy and exact state; separately scoped NIP-17 private conversations.||\nea3f|ea3fa076028c0ab66922043211aad618ed24148b07feb775dc8377f0cac8350a||NIP-49 primitives, normalization and bounded owner-approved ncryptsec import/export.||\na2a7|a2a7f6d3df41bb39bb39c9918783f7e2ee64f9845101c843da987cbcf1a968ef||Advertise only target/profile behavior backed by executable positive and negative evidence.||\nf960|f960d9f8595cc3cebff5b8a4e54bdaebb7d7aab8aba5bdc8aa91a81bc6d391ae||Define core-read/write, phone-signer, openagents-host, Block identity/channel/private-agent and optional backup profiles. Record target/source pins, implementation/evidence, original/decoded/frame/tag/queue/storage limits and compatibility. Reconcile existing proto vs proposed JSON vs socket limits without claiming universal Nostr limits.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/nostr.md\\n- proto/nostr/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Machine-readable matrix rejects unsupported advertised support and inconsistent consumer bounds\\.Boundary fixtures demonstrate clean refusals; profiles name real consumers and optional official NIPs|\n0af2|0af201f17a9bfe5ec818d8381f113abde09d11db27d2cb9d7382421edc82ae8b||Specify and implement a narrow inspectable source/dataflow policy for secret entry points. Reject unsupported constructs, secret branches/indices and calls to public-only _vartime code. Do not advertise #secret syntax before it exists.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/crypto/\\n- tools/coax-nostr/secret-check/\\n- coax/spec.md|Negative fixtures for secret branch/index/callee and unsupported flow are rejected\\.Accepted masked operations execute in checked/optimized modes; scope and gaps are documented|\na974|a974ab76037ce09c8fa121eef14c3e0391f8dedeead01acb5aca71a93fe59a2f||Build on the shipped parser without reopening its completed task. Enforce per-consumer decoded/raw limits and duplicate-key refusal in signed event/JWS/envelope domains; narrow safe-integer projection to 2^53-1 where required. Preserve raw/original numeric bytes and choose explicit error/unknown policy.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/json.coax\\n- coax/lib/nostr/adapters/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Duplicate escaped/equivalent object keys and ambiguous security-critical fields refuse in domain adapters\\.(2^53-1), 2^53, raw numeric retention and mismatched content/frame/proto limits follow the selected profile\\.Existing parser vectors remain compatible except explicitly versioned consumer admission|\n89fb|89fbf9669c3547dd4b8ee09cbaf3fa3637207ba28aac6e0f5305a514cdfb64b1||Define secure_zero with observable stores and bounded scratch/copy/ABI rules. A value barrier alone does not preserve erasure. Inspect optimized/LTO objects with no post-wipe test observation; cover errors, cancellation and aliases.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/crypto/zeroize.coax\\n- coax/src/emit_c.cpp\\n- tools/coax-nostr/zeroize/|Native/Wasm optimized artifacts retain required wipe stores under declared toolchains\\.Injected omitted wipe/early-return/copy escape fails; unsupported erasure guarantees are explicit|\nbab4|bab4ebdf1885f4daff16134a84746e75069c4ec059599aeca0ed36d81fd31c99||Separate event building/signing from nostr-event read-only verification. Caller provides explicit aux/nonce entropy; bind identity/body/preimage and verify produced signature before release. No browser-host dependency in pure module.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/event.coax\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|10000 independent signed-event round trips agree including Unicode and empty fields\\.Bad signer output, invalid key and partial failure release no event or secret scratch|\nda6b|da6baea16717cfc249279b3171348c9ef1cfbc1ff375129ec540e1a003019e93||Define explicit entropy/auxiliary inputs, errors and test injection. OS/browser adapters fail closed, chunk browser requests and never substitute clock/PRNG bytes. Low-level Coax algorithms remain host-independent.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/crypto/\\n- apps/openagents-ios/\\n- coax/web/host.js|Native/iOS/browser absence/short/invalid-span/oversize cases fail without output\\.Deterministic entropy is only available through test adapters|\n6b36|6b36d582af76c4241292a79c9d6ea62bf1e5769a8e0e89b0369261e9120ab3ac||Shared signer request/result/cancel contract with requested identity/body/target/scope, bounded IDs/deadlines, verified output and explicit approvals. Pure decisions with thin NIP-07 effect adapter; supports test keys before production approval.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/keys.coax\\n- coax/web/host.js\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Independent/fake signer output tampering, wrong identity/body, duplicate/late replies and denial are refused\\.Local test slot and NIP-07 adapter implement same bounded lifecycle; no default persistent browser nsec|\n2cde|2cde7e69bb1819ba116e9a3ac85164cbd3692bdab3cf432e05c4287d0acc846b||Specify KDF/salt/domain-separated keys/nonces, authenticated version/length/MAC input, failure/capacity/work limits and old/new readers. Keep existing AES-GCM until independently reviewed replacement and rollback. No unproven same-security claim.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/nostr.md\\n- docs/protocol/\\n- coax/web/unlock/|Independent format review pins exact bytes/algorithms and resolves findings before implementation\\.Immutable old/new/wrong-MAC/nonce/version vectors and staged rollback window documented|\nf116|f11651a6e6639b11287973949ffd2df6240d2b17b9f836c379b3c564404466a1||Execute the same pinned full-vector corpus and malformed-input cases through actual emitted checked/optimized C, Chrome/Safari/Firefox Wasm and iOS C ABI. Device unavailable is an explicit owner step, not silently passed.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- tools/coax-nostr/vectors.sh\\n- coax/tests/nostr/\\n- apps/openagents-ios/Tests/\\n- docs/verification/|Artifact/input hashes and per-target results agree; seeded wrong output is detected\\.Simulator and physical-device results are separate; missing required targets prevent cutover|\n8d2f|8d2ff95ec55aa83a06787d8a6b4539b66ab9376ef370f086271eba8e0284e01d||Audit generated objects for scalar multiplication, sign, ECDH, MAC compare and erasure across arm64/x86-64 and wasm profiles. Pin compiler/toolchain/flags/LTO/artifact hashes; browser JIT results are bounded observations.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- tools/coax-nostr/codegen/\\n- docs/verification/|Seeded branch/index/removed-wipe faults fail the inspection pipeline\\.Target/profile reports identify unsupported claims and record real browser execution|\n4163|4163241dc173e0d4928a42d2a311d4f7f24d5f826d546de53166bfa75f7381fc||Independent reviewers assess arithmetic bounds, group exceptions, nonce/signing, serialization, protocols, erasure and compiler/host boundaries. Resolve findings and pin exact reviewed source/artifact evidence. Self-review and mutation/timing scores are not substitutes.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- docs/verification/\\n- coax/nostr.md|Review report names independent reviewers and reviewed hashes; no unresolved blocking findings\\.Changing reviewed crypto/compiler/ABI inputs invalidates the affected approval rather than silently inheriting it|\n7c36|7c36f2ad5989e170e4f0ad16d4364d26552f425e1c1d8a2901ade823b702bcc5||Bound semantic method/kind/target/scope permissions, replay/correlation, one-use connect, switch_relays/logout, denial/expiry, foreground approval and suspended-phone timeout. Client/signer/user identities remain distinct.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/nip46.coax\\n- apps/openagents-ios/Tests/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Independent transcript tests cover reused secret, revoked permission, replay, switched relay and logout\\.Suspension/resume/late approval cannot sign an expired or differently scoped request|\n2154|21546dbf32d4baa077745f367e0479403200f9fd9a7818cd6ccbbb28c11f77b4||Complete production HTTP sessions after signed login: atomic replay window across restarts/workers, fixation/CSRF policy, scoped roles, cookie rotation, expiry, logout/revocation and cleanup. Login does not imply administration.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/nip98.coax\\n- tools/coax-nostr/server/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Concurrent replay accepts once; restart within window cannot replay\\.Wrong-origin/CSRF/fixation/stale cookie and revoked role fail; valid sign-out removes authorization|\n0653|06535d9a588f918825cfdc1933bdb04889463f38afd9c9536dd9c98f992dbaac||Gate production identities and removal of working paths on independent review, required target/device evidence, real consumer tests, versioned migration flags and rollback. Test-key development remains unblocked; production identity is never silently introduced.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- docs/verification/\\n- coax/nostr.md\\n- coax/web/deploy.sh|Reviewed source/artifact identities, required owner evidence and staged real-consumer results are pinned\\.Rollout/rollback is exercised and changed trusted inputs invalidate affected approvals\\.No self-approved review or unavailable target is counted as passed|\n2ff9|2ff91a54d334072f24d53f39ff1b9f5583227e6d28ae8436a1dca3d7a8a8ab49||Use existing generated root proto codecs in real domains; preserve original Nostr/JWS/HOST bytes, compare projections and enforce bounds/presence/unknown policy. DTOs grant no authority and protobuf bytes never replace signature preimages.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/adapters/\\n- proto/nostr/\\n- proto/tools/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Actual source fixtures round-trip original bytes through generated codecs; mismatched projections refuse\\.Policy tests show decoded owner/verified-like unknown flags cannot authorize an effect|\nf891|f8911d325faba58c113fd1ddc197d948930158f9c35f2e673d200aa7a0beae38||Select exact supported asymmetric algorithms and key-source transports before adding crypto. Bind community Host, issuer, audience, token class/time/TTL; bounded kid/key lookup, pinned authenticated JWKS rotation/cache/revocation and SSRF rules. HOST JOSE profile may reuse primitives but not identity authority.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/block/\\n- proto/nostr/block/fi/\\n- docs/protocol/|Unknown issuer/community, symmetric/none/confused algorithms and unavailable policy fail closed before network lookup\\.JWKS redirect/rebinding/stale/oversize/revoked-key fixtures deny under declared transport policy|\nbd06|bd060841dfcb7edde82e6541dfa18b3be363b71117ebb9927e505fd64507f7c0||Implement only the reviewed FI/HOST asymmetric algorithm profiles (P-256, Ed25519 or RSA as explicitly selected). Bounded compact JWS and base64url parser preserves exact signing input; verify signatures before using claims. This is outside Schnorr-only Nostr core.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/crypto/\\n- coax/lib/nostr/block/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Independent official/negative vectors for selected algorithms and JOSE encodings pass on each advertised target\\.Algorithm/key confusion, malformed tokens, wrong audience/class/time and unverified claims never authorize\\.No unsupported JWT algorithm is advertised|\nd742|d742c2c16829b44d4b0a55f1ccd2f718f0b43200fa56ac73467b07cb8d93b81c||Verify original signed invitations/grants with explicit selected signature/JOSE profile; issuer/audience/host/operation scope, redemption, expiry, revocation epochs and replay. No relay/tailnet membership substitutes for grant authority. Its JOSE allowlist is explicitly selected and reviewed, not inferred from FI or Nostr key possession.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/host/\\n- proto/openagents/host/\\n- nips/openagents/NIP-HOST.md|Wrong host/audience/scope, expired/revoked/replayed grant and unavailable policy refuse before effect\\.A valid least-privilege throwaway grant admits one bounded operation; original evidence is retained|\n62d9|62d9ab1a2b0592cc24cbb1038fd971ca3a3c08035f483dbefb45828227907a01||Verify exact owner-attestation conditions, current owner roles, key possession and AA membership policy. Community admission is independent of host grants; revocation applies to both owner and agent.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/block/\\n- proto/nostr/block/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Altered/reordered condition, wrong owner, revoked/banned owner/agent and stale proof refuse\\.Independent source fixtures exercise direct vs virtual membership and timestamp-vs-kind login policy|\n1df7|1df760017477910e7f4556907ae3017acec29a6a87eaba50482f1efc27172108||Implement WORK/COORD/CAP/POL resource/grant admission with worker keys, all-or-none revision CAS, fences, renew/release, expiry and reconciliation. Preserve old project-key display-name comments as historical notices only.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/host/\\n- proto/openagents/coordination/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Two authenticated workers racing overlapping files get exactly one grant; stale fence cannot commit\\.Lease expiry/reconnect/revocation reconciles before reassignment; display-name comments grant nothing|\n8eb5|8eb5c7c4c49a811844398ae08949e485fba7cfacf8db2e5da62bcd6bc1483040||Persist immutable originals plus bounded indexes. Implement NIP-01 replacement/ties, NIP-09 authorized deletion and NIP-40 expiration, schema migration and crash/reload without resurrecting records or leaking private data.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/store.coax\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Reordered/duplicate/same-time/invalid-deletion/expired transcripts converge with independent expected state\\.Restart/migration/quotas preserve originals and tombstones; unverified events cannot enter store|\n845e|845e5bc9b37cdabad4596ef3fd6f07747f075c31384241214085d758ec1caeb5||Merge verified state across relays; bounded catch-up, duplicate suppression, publish ACK/refusal/unknown status, reconnect and idempotent offline retry. EOSE/short/tied-timestamp pages never prove completeness.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/relay.coax\\n- coax/lib/nostr/store.coax\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Partition/restart/refusal/late-ACK and timestamp-tie tests preserve unknown vs accepted outcomes\\.Missing dependencies/relay disagreement are surfaced; no duplicate effects or false completeness|\na7f8|a7f8c77858d9da382e22e064f08fd5c90d434a4c0f90cd8497cbd940e7216c1f||Validate route/advertisement generation and epoch monotonicity, expiry, rollback protection and authenticated direct-channel binding. Host authorization stays independent of reachable addresses.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/host/\\n- proto/openagents/reach/\\n- nips/openagents/NIP-REACH.md|Reordered old routes, rolled-back epochs, expired advert and wrong peer identity refuse\\.Reconnect/direct and relay fallback preserve identity and never broaden the operation grant|\n8bf1|8bf12873f9a0ecace6e0ea297c52f5b10baaf421c172a371829045d9ddfe1537||Bind WORK/CTX inputs, CAP/POL grants and RUN/SESS journal to one admitted attempt with stable errors/correlation. Preserve original evidence and distinguish running/unknown/failed/completed under reconnect and duplicate delivery.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/host/\\n- apps/openagents-ios/\\n- proto/openagents/|Journal replay/restart converges and cannot execute duplicate requests\\.Revocation mid-run stops new authorized effects and retains truthful partial/unknown result/PR state|\ne43a|e43a80e96fc75e3422c68070c82ef0b026adfe3b464695b8fb6ad19b2672cfb7||Throwaway scoped identity/grant in app -> HOST/REACH over Tailscale -> real Linux Codex task -> streamed progress/result/PR -> fenced completion. Production rollout remains a separate cutover gate.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- apps/openagents-ios/\\n- coax/lib/nostr/host/\\n- docs/verification/|App launch shows actual Linux task progress and resulting PR/evidence\\.Revoked/expired/wrong-scope/replayed request performs no new operation; disconnect outcome remains truthful\\.Retain reproducible local/staging evidence and explicit owner/device steps|\n4f81|4f81c080352e641b3004e36b195b2a3ac1c6344ee42284e221d93fdc54ed8900||Implement adapter login/code exchange/assertion requests with origin/redirect/secret/session binding and bounded retries. FI/FA credentials and identity metadata remain private.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/block/\\n- proto/nostr/block/fa/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Wrong origin/redirect/code/replayed secret/token class/session expiry refuse\\.Credentials never enter public discovery, errors or snapshots|\n4d3e|4d3eb503e0aa63373dd9f87b06b449760f958cd14b14385f5098cf7f161da358||Add currently absent Block projections and remaining supported official behavior shapes only for named consumers; preserve pins, originals, presence/unknowns and immutable published snapshots. Reserved ER/PMA remain unsupported.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- proto/nostr/\\n- proto/tools/\\n- coax/lib/nostr/adapters/|Source/hash/profile closure and protoc interoperability pass for new alpha packages\\.NIP-GS git signing and project MP/PL/RS consumers have explicit acceptance; reserved text does not advertise runtime|\n2f8c|2f8cec664c81b0359e27938bf06515cdd8356139b55393ad07a140e615b8e8ca||Live channel/member/owner read-write admission, viewer-private hidden-channel state and profile commands. Visibility is not membership revocation; unknown metadata never authorizes.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/block/\\n- proto/nostr/block/cl/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Cross-owner/channel/private/system/unlisted/hidden cases fail closed correctly\\.Revocation changes next read/write decision and private visibility never reaches public snapshot|\n078f|078f8095591fcd1060758845d07f2adcdd3a60090b096c3e21c9ebd1a9e84ce0||Timestamp+ID cursors, row/depth/window budgets, bound request/signer evidence, ordering and explicit exhaustion. Missing bounds or short relay pages never prove completion.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/block/\\n- proto/nostr/block/cw/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Tied timestamps, reply depth, moving windows and missing pages return deterministic continuation\\.Wrong viewer/request/relay evidence refuses; no private row leaks through pagination|\n8211|821121005cfd0e865ceefc2c26b965c5e010af9cec8ff6f0a4c06b9787f4594f||Transactional create/update/move/delete with exact original evidence, prev/root identity, idempotence, read visibility and retention. A decoded revision does not pass CAS.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/block/\\n- proto/nostr/block/ar/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Concurrent prev revisions admit once; duplicate same revision is idempotent\\.Wrong root/home/owner/stale prev, deleted and invisible records refuse; replay preserves history|\ne51b|e51b75829f623aee3ecf1fd09aef5231638f636da3f8bb5b739514257f983c80||Implement request/delta/snapshot archive semantics with actor/owner/request binding, consent and relay-scoped UI state. Archiving does not transfer authorship, revoke access or replace channel policy.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/block/\\n- proto/nostr/block/ia/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Wrong actor/owner/request, absent consent and reordered snapshot/delta cases refuse\\.Two clients converge without leaking private archive state|\n1b82|1b8222d7b3a5a157e21f019432ac06adb2749a233e32a4c9ebfeb6756cc84e1c||Enforce owner-bound encrypted AE memory, blinded addressing, null tombstones and private plaintext lifetime. Signature precedes decryption; original encrypted evidence remains available for replay.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/block/\\n- proto/nostr/block/ae/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Independent source fixtures cover valid/tombstone/missing/wrong owner and replay\\.Decrypted body never enters public snapshots or logs; errors wipe owned scratch|\n463e|463ea5a00d626e7299ba5f221f7eba353d8779fe7df8fcaecd3a3673a7e90a9f||Resolve nullable/missing/deleted/unavailable persona/settings/team config with versioned AR-backed snapshots and portable command policy. Unknown or unavailable configuration cannot grant execution.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/block/\\n- proto/nostr/block/ap/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Source fixtures cover null/missing/deleted/unknown config and revision changes\\.Untrusted persona/command fields cannot broaden CAP/POL/HOST authority|\n440e|440e08c1d03f1c849434d91a114e94c2fa3cc48ea1450788f72b3d15751a48c7||Recipient-bound seq/time/correlation/direction checks and bounded live observation. Ephemeral frames are not persisted, indexed or logged, including debug/error paths. Controls require separate operation authority.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/block/\\n- proto/nostr/block/ao/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Wrong recipient/direction/replay/unknown control refuses; authorized observer reconnect respects consent\\.Persistence/log interception proves plaintext observer frames never enter storage or public telemetry|\n6589|658931ee24a6c4894197e1424b888f4f6610127b10e7f50bff273de0eaa189a3||Preserve exact usage/cost decimals, omitted-vs-zero cache fields, cumulative turn/session sequence and independent pricing identity. Metrics are private facts, not inferred payments or grants.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/block/\\n- proto/nostr/block/am/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Large counters/decimal/source omissions and duplicate/out-of-order cumulative metrics retain exact values\\.No float rounding, inferred price or plaintext public snapshot leakage|\n0e58|0e5853c814759a5d56136a7862b8bce10e1d2cd446ba52c642f1dddf0f6a107f||scrypt/Salsa20/8, HChaCha20/XChaCha20 and Poly1305 plus exact NFKC normalization contract, bounded memory/work and erasure. Only required for the optional encrypted-backup profile.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/crypto/\\n- coax/tests/vectors/\\n- tools/coax-nostr/|Independent vectors and normalization cases pass across advertised native/iOS/Wasm targets\\.Untrusted memory/KDF parameters refuse within declared budget; error paths wipe buffers|\nfd45|fd45092f132a11f4b6d2f39553e6ee07dcf9ea44fe71c36d85c445de71c2cdc6||Standard ncryptsec framing and device/browser/native adapters; never substitute a homemade key-wrap format. Explicit approval and resource limits, no public key-backup publication or default plaintext IndexedDB.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/keys.coax\\n- apps/openagents-ios/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Official cross-implementation encrypt/decrypt plus wrong password/version/capacity/normalization vectors pass\\.Owner denial and failure leave no private output or persisted plaintext; optional profile is separately advertised|\nc7e6|c7e6cd613a998f2244c42e7b29defc28ce85da9afb4fe99a50cd8fa07ddc4815||Add NIP-11 relay capabilities and NIP-65 discovery profiles after core merging; enumerate other official NIPs only with actual consumers. Relay metadata and advertised support are untrusted hints, never authority.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/\\n- proto/nostr/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Malformed/stale/conflicting relay metadata and unsupported features produce bounded fallback/refusal\\.Support matrix identifies implemented optional behavior and independent negative fixtures|\n862f|862fbef7ad41dc680b78ea87bb7ad06a033b5e7df36a216f2bd8a14e97148113||Define actual app private messaging over NIP-44/59 with recipient binding, replay/duplicate handling, bounded private history, relay selection and privacy limits; no claim of forward secrecy.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/\\n- apps/openagents-ios/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Independent two-client send/receive/offline/tamper and recipient-isolation cases pass\\.Private bodies never appear in public project data or telemetry; unsupported messaging profiles remain hidden|\n72ed|72ed1e576734883db439e6a0b0fe4868cbcabc206b2d2c556c3be4c15ce4bbb9||Publish per-profile/target/source/evidence support matrix, version migrations and deliberate unsupported features. Schema/text inventory cannot satisfy runtime evidence. Host/channel production cutover must add domain-specific review, not inherit crypto approval as authorization proof.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/nostr.md\\n- docs/verification/\\n- coax/tests/nostr/|Native/browser/iOS profile consumers and negative authority/privacy/replay cases pass with pinned artifacts\\.A planted advertised-but-unimplemented feature fails release; optional backup/messaging only advertised with own evidence\\.New HOST/FI algorithms, authority policies and optional NIP-49 primitives require their own independent source/artifact review before production; initial core-crypto approval is not inherited|\n0a4f|0a4f8e6a861185d1fb708aee6cb2645c2c41df205f90142463dcf04f6f616f69||The handoff reports fail/ct_view.coax now hits E0383 for a local returned borrow before it can exercise E0409. Replace the fixture with a safe borrowed-parameter case that still reaches E0409. Do not just change the expected diagnostic or weaken the lifetime check.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/tests/fail/ct_view.coax\\n- coax/tests/|Focused fixture reaches E0409 for a non-local-borrow compile-time view\\.Existing E0383 local-return cases remain refused; run only affected diagnostic tests|\n";
COAX_WORK_STEPS :: "READ|/projects/coax/index.md\nRELAY|wss://relay.openagents.com\nTASKS|kind 1621, #a 30621:9ef92e341b43...\nORDER|kind 30623, d coax\nTAKE|a NIP-22 comment on the issue: [\"claim\", NAME]\nPLAN|[\"plan\", \"openagents.task-plan.v1\"]: your to-do list\nNOTE|comments on the issue as you go\nDONE|the checks pass; [\"commit\", HASH], status 1631\n";
